Subject: dialog: viewport size, strong scrim, flush body, contained failures

What: `size: "viewport"`, `scrim: "strong"`, `flush` (content runs to the card's
edge), `aria-label` for a title-less dialog (Kobalte names a dialog only from a
mounted Title; axe aria-dialog-name), `onEscapeKeyDown`, class style hooks, and the
dialog host wraps each dialog in an ErrorBoundary.
Why: a dialog mounts from its caller's owner, so a throw inside one reached the
application's boundary: opening Settings on a backend whose consent endpoint
answers 404 replaced the whole app with the error page.

